    {
      "type": "listeningComp",
      "audioUrl": "/audio/unit-23/testimonio-aurora.mp3",
      "transcript": "Yo trabajaba allí desde hace veinte años. Todo era igual todos los días. Llegaba a las siete. Limpiaba el camino. A las nueve iba al mercado y volvía a las once. Había dos guardias y siempre estaban en el mismo sitio. Nadie tocaba las piedras, nunca. Pero esa semana algo era distinto: alguien movía las piedras de noche, y por la mañana no estaban donde debían estar.",
      "translation": "I had worked there for twenty years. Everything was the same every day. I arrived at seven. I cleaned the path. At nine I went to the market and came back at eleven. There were two guards and they were always in the same place. Nobody touched the stones, ever. But that week something was different: someone was moving the stones at night, and in the morning they were not where they should have been.",
      "retryHint": "Pista: escucha lo que era normal y lo que cambió esa semana.",
